  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Electronic Education for Gaza University Students</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Electronic Education for Gaza University Students

The project intends to provide educational services for the displaced university students of Gaza, by offering electronic courses in arts and related  fields. Currently, no universities are operating in Gaza, their faculty members are also displaced, injured or killed and all records are missing. As a first phase of one year comprised of three semesters (summer, fall and winter), Dar al-Kalima will offer courses to students in their final year to ensure their graduation and thus give them some hope for the present and the future.

Since the majority of the students have very limited access to internet services, the sessions for each course will be taped and posted on a digital platform to allow the students to access during any time internet availability is secured. This approach will also ensure offering the courses to as many students as possible. The expectation is that at least 1500 students will benefit from this initiative.</narrative>
  </description>
